# ER043 Normalized Capture — Hub-and-Spoke and Cascading-Submission Audit 5

## Receipt status

Complete substantive capture of the fifth and final announced publication-strategy audit. ER043 proposes a two-paper hub (architecture plus theorem atlas), application spokes using a Minimal Working Realization of the canonical equation, audience-specific venue routing, a three-wave preprint/submission sequence, anti-salami-slicing safeguards, independent computational artifacts, and a later definitive monograph.

## Main recommendations

1. Organize Papers 1–2 as a hub and Papers 3–5 as core spokes, with Papers 6–7 gated downstream extensions.
2. Require each spoke to reproduce only the minimal canonical realization needed for its own question.
3. Route papers to distinct epistemic communities.
4. Use staged submissions to reduce circular-review deadlocks.
5. Give every paper an autonomous research question and its own computational or empirical artifacts.
6. Use concise, explicit programme cross-references rather than repetitive ontology.
7. Reintegrate the peer-reviewed series into a non-reprint research monograph.
